WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.000
- Hey, everybody!

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:03.290
Welcome to the first official episode

00:00:03.290 --> 00:00:04.600
of the Wednesday Checkup.

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:06.247
I have my puppy, Bear, oh--

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:08.990
Is he still in the shot
when he's like this?

00:00:08.990 --> 00:00:11.006
I have to tell you a crazy story

00:00:11.006 --> 00:00:12.930
of something that happened to us

00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:14.260
just a few days ago.

00:00:14.260 --> 00:00:16.040
At the end of this video
I'm gonna be giving

00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:18.320
you tips on how to protect yourself

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:20.230
in case a dog attacks you and how

00:00:20.230 --> 00:00:22.190
to break up a dog fight if your dog gets

00:00:22.190 --> 00:00:23.190
into a fight with another.

00:00:23.190 --> 00:00:24.830
All right, let me get to the story.

00:00:24.830 --> 00:00:26.410
Bear will come back a little bit later

00:00:26.410 --> 00:00:27.560
and say bye to you guys.

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.300
A few days ago, I was filming

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:30.950
for the YouTube channel, surprise!

00:00:30.950 --> 00:00:32.100
I'm not gonna tell you the video.

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:33.720
It's gonna be out later this month.

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:35.406
And I decided to take Bear downstairs

00:00:35.406 --> 00:00:36.470
to the dog park.

00:00:36.470 --> 00:00:38.350
Bear's there twice a day at least

00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:40.080
so he knows all the other dogs.

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:41.534
He plays really well, especially

00:00:41.534 --> 00:00:44.900
with the little Chihuahuas and Frenchies.

00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:46.210
There's even one that looks

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:47.846
like a Wookie.

00:00:47.846 --> 00:00:48.970
(wookie noise)

00:00:48.970 --> 00:00:50.430
He loves it, he's in heaven,

00:00:50.430 --> 00:00:51.263
they're all in heaven,

00:00:51.263 --> 00:00:52.760
all the owners know Bear.

00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:53.900
I get to the dog park,

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:56.970
I see a young lady come in
with a Golden Retriever.

00:00:56.970 --> 00:00:59.050
First little suspicious sign is

00:00:59.050 --> 00:01:01.050
her Golden Retriever pulled her in

00:01:01.050 --> 00:01:02.460
to the dog park.

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:04.237
I was like "All right she
doesn't have great control

00:01:04.237 --> 00:01:05.070
"of her dog."

00:01:05.070 --> 00:01:06.080
and I watch these things.

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:07.470
I wanna know right away if there's

00:01:07.470 --> 00:01:08.720
a problem dog coming in,

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:09.780
so I have to hold Bear,

00:01:09.780 --> 00:01:11.100
make sure that he doesn't get hurt.

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:11.960
It still looked friendly,

00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:14.390
tail was wagging and
it's a Golden Retriever

00:01:14.390 --> 00:01:15.223
at the end of the day, you know.

00:01:15.223 --> 00:01:17.500
And right away she tells me that

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:20.370
her dog doesn't really like big dogs

00:01:20.370 --> 00:01:21.620
and is kinda afraid of them.

00:01:21.620 --> 00:01:23.840
Bear said hi to that dog,

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:25.500
and it gave him like a little pause

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:27.440
and Bear just continued
along his merry way

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:28.460
playing with the other dogs.

00:01:28.460 --> 00:01:30.030
So about five minutes go by,

00:01:30.030 --> 00:01:32.360
all of a sudden I see that Bear

00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:34.310
is standing right next to the Golden

00:01:34.310 --> 00:01:35.350
side by side.

00:01:35.350 --> 00:01:37.610
But they're showing all
the signs of aggression.

00:01:37.610 --> 00:01:39.440
Frozen, mouths closed,

00:01:39.440 --> 00:01:41.250
slobbering, tails up,

00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:42.460
very rigid pose.

00:01:42.460 --> 00:01:44.005
The other dog owner comes over

00:01:44.005 --> 00:01:46.649
and sort of shoves her dog away from Bear.

00:01:46.649 --> 00:01:48.650
And that triggers the Golden.

00:01:48.650 --> 00:01:51.510
Snarling, and the Golden
just dives at Bear.

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:52.907
I initially was like

00:01:52.907 --> 00:01:55.077
"Okay, a dog fight, I've seen these happen

00:01:55.077 --> 00:01:57.010
"I know how to break this up, no worries."

00:01:57.010 --> 00:01:59.360
As soon as I run up to
control the situation,

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:01.750
she grabs her dog's collar.

00:02:01.750 --> 00:02:03.340
It was a big Golden Retriever

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:05.560
it was probably like 95 pounds.

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:07.960
She ends up falling with
the Golden Retriever

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:09.560
'cause there's a little mound in the park,

00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:12.190
and she falls onto the
concrete holding the Golden.

00:02:12.190 --> 00:02:13.690
The lady starts screaming.

00:02:13.690 --> 00:02:17.300
Her Golden is locked on her forearm.

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:18.850
Her own Golden Retriever.

00:02:18.850 --> 00:02:21.292
She's screaming "It's me, it's me!"

00:02:21.292 --> 00:02:22.810
crying for help.

00:02:22.810 --> 00:02:25.670
Two people from the street
jump the fence of the dog park,

00:02:25.670 --> 00:02:27.420
start punching her dog in the face

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:28.700
to get it to let go 'cause it's,

00:02:28.700 --> 00:02:30.210
I mean this is a big dog and

00:02:30.210 --> 00:02:32.560
it's completely like smashing her forearm.

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:35.270
Finally it lets go, but
as soon as it lets go

00:02:35.270 --> 00:02:37.780
it gets angry and jumps on her again.

00:02:37.780 --> 00:02:39.182
Luckily all the people that were there

00:02:39.182 --> 00:02:41.139
they were able to control
it with the collar,

00:02:41.139 --> 00:02:43.080
pulling on it's legs, it's neck.

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:45.930
Pulled up her sweater
and showed me her wounds,

00:02:45.930 --> 00:02:48.100
and she had deep puncture wounds

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:50.000
at least three deep puncture
wounds what it seemed like.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:52.370
And some smaller cuts as well,

00:02:52.370 --> 00:02:53.910
and bleeding from the nose and head.

00:02:53.910 --> 00:02:54.743
And she's like "Well, I don't need

00:02:54.743 --> 00:02:56.410
"to go to the hospital for this."

00:02:56.410 --> 00:02:58.817
and I'm like "You really
need to see a doctor."

00:02:58.817 --> 00:03:00.977
"You don't know if you have an infection.

00:03:00.977 --> 00:03:02.837
"You don't know if you're
gonna continue bleeding.

00:03:02.837 --> 00:03:05.720
"You need probably
stitches and antibiotics."

00:03:05.720 --> 00:03:08.470
My adrenaline at that point
was just through the roof,

00:03:08.470 --> 00:03:10.860
I've seen dogs get into fights many times,

00:03:10.860 --> 00:03:11.693
it just happens.

00:03:11.693 --> 00:03:13.260
You know, dogs are animals,

00:03:13.260 --> 00:03:14.500
you have to correct them sometimes.

00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:16.865
And I've even seen dogs
accidentally bite humans

00:03:16.865 --> 00:03:19.400
when humans would put their hands

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:20.450
in the middle of a dog fight.

00:03:20.450 --> 00:03:23.820
But I've never seen a
dog attack another dog,

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:25.540
who first of all wasn't being violent,

00:03:25.540 --> 00:03:29.056
and then when separated, go after a human,

00:03:29.056 --> 00:03:31.470
but not just any human, it's own human.

00:03:31.470 --> 00:03:33.640
If that dog went for her neck,

00:03:33.640 --> 00:03:35.500
and bit through her jugular vein,

00:03:35.500 --> 00:03:36.333
or carotid artery,

00:03:36.333 --> 00:03:38.170
she could have bled out and died.

00:03:38.170 --> 00:03:40.750
Here's what to do if your
dog gets into a dog fight.

00:03:40.750 --> 00:03:42.730
First, please, whatever you do,

00:03:42.730 --> 00:03:46.122
don't stick your hands,
fingers, arms, legs,

00:03:46.122 --> 00:03:48.230
in between two dogs that are fighting.

00:03:48.230 --> 00:03:49.890
You're just asking to get bitten.

00:03:49.890 --> 00:03:52.200
If you have two dogs that know each other

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:53.519
and they're sort of fighting at home,

00:03:53.519 --> 00:03:56.250
a very simple thing to is
throw a blanket over them.

00:03:56.250 --> 00:03:58.050
That would usually make them disperse.

00:03:58.050 --> 00:04:01.250
If you're in a situation
where you wanna say no

00:04:01.250 --> 00:04:03.190
and be firm and yell at a dog,

00:04:03.190 --> 00:04:04.670
I wouldn't really recommend that.

00:04:04.670 --> 00:04:06.677
Loud voices can actually get the dogs

00:04:06.677 --> 00:04:09.697
even angrier and make them
wanna go at each other more.

00:04:09.697 --> 00:04:12.830
Think about like a boxer
inside a boxing ring,

00:04:12.830 --> 00:04:13.900
they don't hear people chanting,

00:04:13.900 --> 00:04:14.840
they're just in the zone.

00:04:14.840 --> 00:04:16.904
But on the off chance
if you have something

00:04:16.904 --> 00:04:18.500
like an air horn that makes

00:04:18.500 --> 00:04:20.070
a really loud high pitched noise

00:04:20.070 --> 00:04:22.170
it can be loud enough
to disperse the fight.

00:04:22.170 --> 00:04:23.710
Now the most effective way

00:04:23.710 --> 00:04:25.458
to separate two dogs that are fighting

00:04:25.458 --> 00:04:27.080
requires two people.

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:29.520
One on either side, behind the dogs.

00:04:29.520 --> 00:04:31.280
You wanna pick up the hind legs,

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:33.290
and do something known as
a wheelbarrow technique.

00:04:33.290 --> 00:04:35.000
As soon as you lift up the hind legs,

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:36.790
generally the dogs will wanna let go

00:04:36.790 --> 00:04:38.010
because they don't know what's going on.

00:04:38.010 --> 00:04:39.441
But as soon as you lift up the dogs

00:04:39.441 --> 00:04:42.160
try and move in a circular fashion.

00:04:42.160 --> 00:04:43.970
As you move in a circular fashion,

00:04:43.970 --> 00:04:45.650
it'll give the dogs something to do,

00:04:45.650 --> 00:04:47.526
but be careful because the dog will try

00:04:47.526 --> 00:04:48.749
and kick it's legs out.

00:04:48.749 --> 00:04:50.710
You really need to get a solid grip,

00:04:50.710 --> 00:04:52.220
and you don't wanna get bitten.

00:04:52.220 --> 00:04:54.690
Now what if the dog attacks you?

00:04:54.690 --> 00:04:57.390
First of all, do not run whatever you do.

00:04:57.390 --> 00:05:00.187
Dogs are very fast, and they
have a natural prey drive

00:05:00.187 --> 00:05:01.950
that makes them wanna chase.

00:05:01.950 --> 00:05:03.865
Stand up tall, stand sideways,

00:05:03.865 --> 00:05:05.443
and not make eye contact.

00:05:05.443 --> 00:05:07.450
So it's not confrontational.

00:05:07.450 --> 00:05:09.470
You do still wanna keep an eye on the dog

00:05:09.470 --> 00:05:10.810
without making eye contact.

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:14.820
Next in a firm voice, you
wanna tell the dog "No."

00:05:14.820 --> 00:05:17.150
you just have to say it very passionately,

00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:19.490
confident that you're willing
to stand your own ground.

00:05:19.490 --> 00:05:21.552
At the same time, you wanna make fists.

00:05:21.552 --> 00:05:23.010
And it's not because I want you

00:05:23.010 --> 00:05:24.570
to get ready to fight the dog,

00:05:24.570 --> 00:05:27.140
but it's because the
first things to get bitten

00:05:27.140 --> 00:05:28.416
and bitten off are fingers.

00:05:28.416 --> 00:05:30.200
If you keep them in fists,

00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:31.740
you're less likely to lose a finger.

00:05:31.740 --> 00:05:33.460
If the dog doesn't care that you

00:05:33.460 --> 00:05:36.050
tried to stand non-confrontationally,

00:05:36.050 --> 00:05:37.208
not make eye contact,
and gave it a command,

00:05:37.208 --> 00:05:39.950
and it still attacks you,

00:05:39.950 --> 00:05:42.350
at this point you have to
do what you have to do.

00:05:42.350 --> 00:05:43.790
Punch the dog in the nose,

00:05:43.790 --> 00:05:44.900
hit it in its throat,

00:05:44.900 --> 00:05:47.050
those are its two most sensitive areas.

00:05:47.050 --> 00:05:48.870
If you can kick it in the ribcage

00:05:48.870 --> 00:05:50.090
that's another thing you can do.

00:05:50.090 --> 00:05:51.790
And if you're completely losing the fight,

00:05:51.790 --> 00:05:53.160
make sure to roll up

00:05:53.160 --> 00:05:55.060
and protect your sensitive areas.

00:05:55.060 --> 00:05:56.530
Your throat, and face.

00:05:56.530 --> 00:05:58.310
If you're able to wrestle with the dog

00:05:58.310 --> 00:05:59.760
and get on top of it and pin it,

00:05:59.760 --> 00:06:01.970
know that the only way a
dog can really hurt you

00:06:01.970 --> 00:06:02.890
is with it's mouth.

00:06:02.890 --> 00:06:05.059
By getting on top of the
dog and pinning it down,

00:06:05.059 --> 00:06:07.100
you can really neutralize the threat

00:06:07.100 --> 00:06:08.170
of the dog biting you.

00:06:08.170 --> 00:06:09.710
While you're fighting off this dog

00:06:09.710 --> 00:06:11.136
you're also yelling for help

00:06:11.136 --> 00:06:13.190
in the hopes that other people hear you

00:06:13.190 --> 00:06:14.200
and come to your aid.

00:06:14.200 --> 00:06:15.296
If the dog runs away

00:06:15.296 --> 00:06:17.110
or you're able to get away,

00:06:17.110 --> 00:06:18.430
call for help right away,

00:06:18.430 --> 00:06:20.100
and you need to go see a doctor.

00:06:20.100 --> 00:06:22.350
You need to make sure your
vaccinations are up to date.

00:06:22.350 --> 00:06:23.669
If it was a rabid dog you may need

00:06:23.669 --> 00:06:25.670
a series of injections.

00:06:25.670 --> 00:06:27.280
You'll probably need antibiotics.

00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:29.530
You may need sutures to stop the bleeding.

00:06:29.530 --> 00:06:31.400
Get help as soon as possible.

00:06:31.400 --> 00:06:32.480
The last thing you wanna do

00:06:32.480 --> 00:06:34.400
is faint because of blood loss,

00:06:34.400 --> 00:06:35.840
and not have anybody help you.

00:06:35.840 --> 00:06:37.391
Once your health is taken care of

00:06:37.391 --> 00:06:40.720
make sure you report the dog
bite to the proper authorities.

00:06:40.720 --> 00:06:42.340
The last thing you want is for that dog

00:06:42.340 --> 00:06:44.130
to bite another person or animal.

00:06:44.130 --> 00:06:46.640
I'm not an animal behavior specialist,

00:06:46.640 --> 00:06:48.552
I do have a lot of
experience in raising dogs

00:06:48.552 --> 00:06:50.870
and understanding when
they're about to get angry

00:06:50.870 --> 00:06:51.780
or do something wrong.

00:06:51.780 --> 00:06:53.530
But even here I was shook.

00:06:53.530 --> 00:06:55.860
I needed to go and look
up some information

00:06:55.860 --> 00:06:57.750
about what to do to refresh my memory,

00:06:57.750 --> 00:07:00.100
so I decided to make
this video for you guys.

00:07:00.100 --> 00:07:01.270
Whether or not you own a dog,

00:07:01.270 --> 00:07:02.870
I think this is useful information.

00:07:02.870 --> 00:07:04.760
If you have any questions
about this story,

00:07:04.760 --> 00:07:06.226
if you have any comments about this story,

00:07:06.226 --> 00:07:08.440
jump in the comments section down below.

00:07:08.440 --> 00:07:11.120
If you want more videos
with my little Bear pup,

00:07:11.120 --> 00:07:11.960
please let me know

00:07:11.960 --> 00:07:13.467
because I'm always down to film with Bear,

00:07:13.467 --> 00:07:14.980
and he loves being on camera.

00:07:14.980 --> 00:07:16.220
And most importantly,

00:07:16.220 --> 00:07:18.598
as always, stay happy, and healthy.

00:07:18.598 --> 00:07:21.265
(serene music)

